/-
Johnson/Unfolds/DeclRecsLit.lean: the different declared rounds of the proof file's IOP as written
in Lean, at the full size, written out: one list of 136 values of `Fmt.DeclaredRound`. Data alone.

A value: the round's entry of the plan ⟨name, count, work, msg, roots, answers, drawE, drawNZ, poss,
logN, trits, rows⟩ · the stored trees that it opens, each ⟨shape, salt, item, lo, count⟩ · the other
trees that it opens, each (shape, whose tree), a shape being ⟨a, W, stored, tree⟩.

Whence. Printed by a program off the three lists of declared rounds (`FileDescription.roundsDeclaredByBlocks`,
Johnson/Desc/Block.lean) of the value of `ProofFile.onlineDescription` at the second hash function and the goals'
stored full-size public files (`VerifierAndGoals.storedPublicFiles`, Ladder/Stored.lean), by Lean's evaluator, and laid
into Lean's notation by a second program. The order is that of a value's first standing along the
first, the shared and the second chain's list: 108 stand in the first list, the shared list brings
21 more, the second 7. NO THEOREM SAYS THAT THESE ARE THAT VALUE's ROUNDS.

How the lists are had back. As runs "how often, which value" the three lists were printed too
(17,108, 43 and 19 runs; 48,293, 68 and 30 rounds). A program held these runs against the text of
`dryProofRunsFull0`, `dryProofRunsFull1`, `dryProofRunsFull2` (Johnson/G/DryProofLit.lean): they
are the same, run for run; and the entry of the value number i here is the entry of the record
number i of `dryProofRecsFull` there. So no second list of runs is written here.

  `declRecsFull`   136 values

-/
